{"kind":"artifact","text":"Documentation repair at exact clean head 2808a1289d0cfac9abcdaac7a54b52eceeb9e43a on request/merge-staleness-docs, cut directly from current main 92125957 so it fast-forwards.\n\nFour passages said gs merge refuses a stale approval or artifact, or that it keeps a \"strict\" reading of staleness. The staleness relaxation at 23c4c759 made that false, and nothing had moved the prose. I verified the current behaviour by reading the code rather than trusting the change log: validateMerge at cmd/gs/main.go:861 reaches liveStatement (:1049) and liveArtifact (:1016), whose standing* helpers refuse only an ineffective or retired record, and whose own comments now read \"Ordinary reasoning staleness is recorded by the merge receipt\". On the independent-review path validateMerge returns reviewStaleness (:753) as a note string, not an error, so ordinary staleness of the approval or the artifact does not block the merge.\n\nChanged in this head: docs/concepts/staleness.md now says merge refuses the retired pointer and lands the stale one, naming describes-a-superseded-world as the exception. docs/reference/gs/merge.md corrects both refusal-table rows, adds \"ineffective\" to the artifact row because standingArtifact does refuse it, replaces the \"strict reading\" passage with a section separating what is recorded from what is refused, and corrects the same claim about co-signed set members at the bottom of the page. docs/concepts/work-loop.md carried the identical wrong claim and was found by audit rather than from the original list; it is corrected the same way.\n\nEvery factual claim the new prose adds was checked against the code at this head, not asserted: the Gitseq-Staleness: trailer exists at cmd/gs/main.go:590 and is appended by mergeReceiptMessage at :614-615; the durable merge assertion carries stale and staleness at cmd/gs/succession.go:458-460; standingArtifact refuses ineffective at cmd/gs/main.go:1000-1002 and retired at :1005-1007; and validateReviewedSet at cmd/gs/succession.go:541 applies liveArtifact to every co-signed member, which is what makes the \"same rule as the primary\" sentence true.\n\ninternal/workroom/fold.go carries one code comment change. The mergeSuccessionPlan comment narrates why the succession mechanism exists, in the past tense throughout except one clause asserting that gs merge refuses a stale successor. That clause is now past tense, so the motivation still reads without asserting a behaviour the code no longer has. No code changed.\n\nGates run at this exact head, all green: go vet ./... exit 0; go build ./... exit 0; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... ok in 44.99s, which is the documentation citation gate and the one that matters here; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 across all 27 packages with none failing. git status --porcelain is empty and the worktree is clean. No rests_on front matter was touched on any page, so no page's anchoring moved.\n\nScope: documentation and one code comment. No behaviour change, no interface change, no test change.\n\nThis artifact covers the three changed pages under docs. The fold.go comment is covered by the companion artifact at internal/workroom standing at this same head.","body":{"commit":"2808a1289d0cfac9abcdaac7a54b52eceeb9e43a","path":"docs"}}